{"id": "unknown-2026-09-26-003", "date": "2026-09-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh extends loan relief deadline for raw jute exporters", "content": "Bangladesh Bank has given raw jute exporters until September 30, 2026 to seek restructuring of classified loans with a 2 per cent down payment.\nBanks have until December 31, 2026 to settle applications under unchanged BRPD circular terms.\nThe move gives distressed jute shippers more time to regularise accounts amid sector-specific financial pressures.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-extends-loan-relief-deadline-for-raw-jute-exporters-313772-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-26-004", "date": "2026-09-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh eases MMF imports: A new route for synthetic apparel?", "content": "Bangladesh has eased imports of specialised synthetic fabrics for seamless sportswear, high-value fashion items and functional apparel.\nIts RMG exports reached $38.70 billion in FY2025–26, or 80.62 per cent of total exports, while most MMF yarns and fibres are imported.\nUS apparel shipments from Bangladesh were about $4.66 billion in January–July 2026, down 6.5 per cent year on year.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-eases-mmf-imports-a-new-route-for-synthetic-apparel--313787-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-26-005", "date": "2026-09-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Canada, Vietnam strengthen trade ties under new Strategic Partnership", "content": "Canada and Vietnam have elevated bilateral ties to a Strategic Partnership, with trade, investment, economic co-operation, transportation and supply-chain management among its core areas. \nBoth sides reaffirmed support for concluding the ASEAN-Canada FTA and strengthening co-operation under the CPTPP.\nVietnam is Canada’s largest trading partner in ASEAN, highlighting the scope for further trade.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/canada-vietnam-strengthen-trade-ties-under-new-strategic-partnership-313781-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-26-006", "date": "2026-09-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.62, "keywords": ["decline", "weak", "pressure", "delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weakness persists in south Indian cotton yarn, prices down in Mumbai", "content": "South Indian cotton yarn market stayed bearish, with Mumbai prices down ₹2–4 per kg amid selling pressure, poor payment conditions and cautious buying.\nTiruppur cotton yarn prices held steady after earlier declines, though mills faced pressure from subdued export demand and falling ICE cotton.\nGujarat cotton fell ₹1,000 per candy as delayed new-crop arrivals were offset by ICE cotton volatility.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weakness-persists-in-south-indian-cotton-yarn-prices-down-in-mumbai-313779-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-26-007", "date": "2026-09-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh gets RCEP go-ahead as accession process moves forward", "content": "Bangladesh has received approval to advance its accession process to RCEP, with an ad hoc working group to expedite negotiations. \nFor apparel and textile supply chains, membership could expand access to major Asian-Pacific markets, help address post-LDC graduation trade challenges, retain preferential market access, strengthen supply-chain integration and attract foreign direct investment (FDI).", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-gets-rcep-go-ahead-as-accession-process-moves-forward-313778-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
